---
import RobotConversation from './RobotConversation.astro';
---
<RobotConversation>
  <Fragment slot="consent">
    <details data-ai-consent>
      <summary>Optional local model</summary>
      <p>The conversation already works on your device. This experiment lets a small model select an exact passage from the same sources. It cannot add facts.</p>
      <p>Enabling it downloads about 204 MB plus runtime files from model hosts. They receive download requests, never your questions. A compatible GPU is required. Files may stay in your browser cache.</p>
      <button type="button" data-enable>Download and enable AI</button>
    </details>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="about">
  <details class="robot-about">
    <summary>About this conversation</summary>
    <p>
      Answers select published resume statements using local search and fixed rules.
      This is a bounded guide to Tim's work, not an open-ended generative chat.
      Sources are self-reported and include historical claims. Each answer's
      source disclosure includes dates, ownership, and limits.
    </p>
    <p>
      The page downloads public records with its code. Searching and answering
      happen in your browser. Questions are never sent to a resume service or
      inference server. Conversation stays in page memory, up to 12 questions.
      Clear starts over. Closing stops pending work and unloads the optional model.
    </p>
    <p>
      The optional model runs on your device with <a
        href="https://github.com/mlc-ai/web-llm"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">WebLLM</a
      >. Model: <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/mlc-ai/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-q4f16_1-MLC"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">MLC SmolLM2 360M</a
      >, using f16 or f32 according to GPU support. WebLLM and the <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">upstream SmolLM2 model</a
      > use Apache 2.0. See publisher pages for license and provenance.
    </p>
  </details>
  </Fragment>
</RobotConversation>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/robot/host';
</script>
